{% block lens %}INTERACTION (IA). For each interactive element: what happens on click/submit (API call, navigation target, modal,
toast, redirect), screen-to-screen transitions (use "transitions"), back/cancel/edit behaviour, side effects (e.g. order
created, cart cleared, OTP re-sent), and for payment/order CTAs what the user sees when the call fails.
Skip the standard Back arrow and the targets of a standard tab bar unless the design makes them non-obvious;
ask instead whether the tab bar should be shown at all inside a checkout or modal step.
Categories: ACTION, NAVIGATION. Owner tech or product.
Do NOT cover field validation, enabled/visible conditions, data sources, or business formulas; other specialists own those.{% endblock %}
